window.ScripturaLexicons.BDAG_PART_0005 = {source:"BDAG", searchAnchorId:"bdag-search-anchor", entryAnchorId:"bdag-entry-anchor", rowsHtml:"<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-agape-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"ἀγάπη agape amor estima afeição consideração refeição comunitária festa de amor BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">ἀγάπη</td><td>Substantivo</td><td>amor; afeição; estima; refeição de comunhão</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr><tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-agapetos-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"ἀγαπητός agapetos amado querido único estimado valorizado Filho Cristo BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">ἀγαπητός</td><td>Adjetivo</td><td>amado; querido; estimado</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr><tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-hagar-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"Ἁγάρ Hagar Agar הָגָר Abraão Ismael Sinai Arábia Gálatas BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">Ἁγάρ</td><td>Nome próprio</td><td>Agar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr><tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-angareuo-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"ἀγγαρεύω angareuo requisitar serviço forçar compelir correio oficial persa BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">ἀγγαρεύω</td><td>Verbo</td><td>requisitar; obrigar ao serviço; forçar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr><tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-angeion-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"ἀγγεῖον angeion vaso frasco recipiente óleo peixe corpo espírito BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">ἀγγεῖον</td><td>Substantivo</td><td>vaso; frasco; recipiente</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr><tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-angelia-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"ἀγγελία angelia mensagem boa notícia evangelho instrução diretiva amor BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">ἀγγελία</td><td>Substantivo</td><td>mensagem; instrução; diretiva</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr><tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-angelikos-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"ἀγγελικός angelikos angélico mensageiro celestial anjo BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">ἀγγελικός</td><td>Adjetivo</td><td>angélico; relativo a mensageiro celestial</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr><tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-angello-bdag\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"ἀγγέλλω angello anunciar mensagem Maria Madalena BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<td class=\"table-lemma greek\">ἀγγέλλω</td><td>Verbo</td><td>anunciar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td>\n</tr>", cardsHtml:"<article id=\"entry-agape-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">ἀγάπη</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"greek\">ης, ἡ</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦agápē⟧</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span>substantivo</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Este termo deixou poucos vestígios na literatura grega politeísta. Uma inscrição sepulcral, provavelmente honrando um oficial militar politeísta que é tido em “alta estima” por sua cidade [SEG VIII, 11, 6 (séc. III d.C.)], lança luz sobre um exemplo como Filodemo, <em>παρρ.</em> col. 13a, 3 Oliv., mas veja Söding [abaixo] 294. As restaurações em POxy 1380, 28 e 109 s. [séc. II d.C.] são discutidas: veja <em>New Docs</em> 4, 259 [literatura]; Söding [fim] 294 s., n. 68 [literatura]. Para outros exemplos do mundo greco-romano, veja Ltzm., exc. após 1 Co 13; L-S-J-M; A. Ceresa-Gastaldo, “Αγάπη nei documenti anteriori al NT”, <em>Aegyptus</em> 31, 1951, 269–306, com um novo exemplo papirológico e uma nova inscrição provenientes de fontes seculares do séc. III d.C.; em <em>RivFil</em> 31, 1953, 347–356, o mesmo autor mostra a palavra restaurada numa inscrição de 27 a.C., mas contra C.-G. veja a literatura em Söding 293, n. 57. Em fontes judaicas: LXX, especialmente SSol, também pseudoepígrafos, Fílon, <em>Deus Imm.</em> 69; Justino, <em>D.</em> 93, 4. Compare A. Carr, <em>ET</em> 10, 1899, 321–330. Sua escassez na literatura grega em geral pode dever-se a um presumido sabor coloquial do substantivo (mas veja IPontEux I, 359, 6 como paralelo a <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.8.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 8.8</a> abaixo). Nenhum estigma semelhante se ligava ao uso do verbo <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπάω\" data-meanings=\"amar\">ἀγαπάω</span> [q.v.].)\n<span class=\"sense-number\">1.</span>\n<strong>A qualidade de consideração calorosa e interesse por outro, estima, afeição, consideração, amor</strong> (sem limitação a relações muito íntimas e, muito raramente no grego geral, de atração sexual).\n<strong>a.</strong> Do amor humano.\n<strong>α.</strong> Sem indicação da pessoa que é objeto do interesse (compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/ECC.9.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ec 9.1</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/ECC.9.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">6</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/SIR.48.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eclo 48.11</a> v.l.):\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"amor\">ἀ.</span> como sujeito:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἡ ἀ. οἰκοδομεῖ\" data-meanings=\"o amor edifica\">ἡ ἀ. οἰκοδομεῖ</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.8.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 8.1</a>. — <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.13.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">13.4</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.13.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">8</a> (sobre 1 Co 13, veja os comentários [Máximo de Tiro 20:2, louvor de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἔρως\" data-meanings=\"eros|amor\">ἔρως</span> — o que ele não é e o que é; A. Harnack, <em>SBBerlAk</em> 1911, 132–163, esp. 152 s.; E. Lehmann e A. Fridrichsen, “1 Cor 13 e. christl.-stoische Diatribe”, <em>StKr Sonderheft</em> 1922, 55–95]; E. Hoffmann, “Pauli Hymnus auf d. Liebe”, <em>Dtsche Vierteljahrsschrift für Literaturwiss. u. Geistesgesch.</em> 4, 1926, 58–73; N. Lund, <em>JBL</em> 50, 1931, 266–276; G. Rudberg, <em>Hellas och Nya Testamentet</em> 1934, 149 s.; H. Riesenfeld, <em>ConNeot</em> 5, 1941, 1–32; <em>Nuntius</em> 6, 1952, 47 s.);\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.1.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fp 1.9</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἡ ἀ. κακὸν οὐκ ἐργάζεται\" data-meanings=\"o amor não pratica o mal\">ἡ ἀ. κακὸν οὐκ ἐργάζεται</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.13.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 13.10</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"πλήρωμα νόμου ἡ ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"o amor é cumprimento da lei\">πλήρωμα νόμου ἡ ἀ.</span> ibid.;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ψυγήσεται ἡ ἀ. τ. πολλῶν\" data-meanings=\"o amor de muitos esfriará\">ψυγήσεται ἡ ἀ. τ. πολλῶν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.24.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 24.12</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἡ ἀ. ἀνυπόκριτος\" data-meanings=\"o amor sem hipocrisia\">ἡ ἀ. ἀνυπόκριτος</span>, <em>que o amor seja genuíno</em>,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.12.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 12.9</a>, compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.6.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 6.6</a>. Como predicado: <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.1.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Tm 1.5</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 4.16b</a> (compare bα). Como objeto:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγάπην ἔχειν\" data-meanings=\"ter amor\">ἀγάπην ἔχειν</span> (Did., <em>Gen.</em> 221, 30)\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.13.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 13.1–3</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.2.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fp 2.2</a>\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φιλίαν ἢ ἀγάπην ἔχοντες\" data-meanings=\"tendo amizade ou amor\">φιλίαν ἢ ἀγάπην ἔχοντες</span> Justino, <em>D.</em> 93, 4;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"διώκειν\" data-meanings=\"buscar|perseguir\">διώκειν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.14.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 14.1</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.6.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Tm 6.11</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TI.2.22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Tm 2.22</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐνδύσασθαι τὴν ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"revestir-se do amor\">ἐνδύσασθαι τὴν ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.3.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 3.14</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀφιέναι\" data-meanings=\"deixar|abandonar\">ἀφιέναι</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.2.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ap 2.4</a>. — <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.1.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pe 1.7</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.1.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 1.8</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐμαρτύρησάν σου τῇ ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"deram testemunho do teu amor\">ἐμαρτύρησάν σου τῇ ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/3JN.1.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3 Jo 6</a>. Atributivamente no genitivo:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὁ κόπος τῆς ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"o labor do amor\">ὁ κόπος τῆς ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.1.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ts 1.3</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τὸ τ. ὑμετέρας ἀ. γνήσιον\" data-meanings=\"a genuinidade do vosso amor\">τὸ τ. ὑμετέρας ἀ. γνήσιον</span>,\n<em>a genuinidade do vosso amor</em>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.8.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 8.8</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἔνδειξις τῆς ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"demonstração do amor\">ἔνδειξις τῆς ἀ.</span> v. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.8.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">24</a>; compare <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"πᾶσαν ἐνδεικνυμένους ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"demonstrando todo amor\">πᾶσαν ἐνδεικνυμένους ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/TIT.2.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tt 2.10</a> v.l. — <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.10.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 10.24</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.2.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fp 2.1</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1PE.5.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Pe 5.14</a>; 1 Cl 49:2. — Em locuções preposicionais:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐξ ἀγάπης\" data-meanings=\"por amor\">ἐξ ἀγάπης</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.1.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fp 1.16</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"παράκλησις ἐπὶ τῇ ἀ. σου\" data-meanings=\"consolo por causa do teu amor\">παράκλησις ἐπὶ τῇ ἀ. σου</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHM.1.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fm 7</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"περιπατεῖν κατὰ ἀ., ἐν ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"andar segundo o amor, em amor\">περιπατεῖν κατὰ ἀ., ἐν ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.14.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 14.15</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.5.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 5.2</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐν ἀ. ἔρχεσθαι\" data-meanings=\"vir em amor\">ἐν ἀ. ἔρχεσθαι</span> (oposto a <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐν ῥάβδῳ\" data-meanings=\"com vara\">ἐν ῥάβδῳ</span>) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.4.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 4.21</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀληθεύειν ἐν ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"falar/praticar a verdade em amor\">ἀληθεύειν ἐν ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.4.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 4.15</a>. Outras combinações verbais com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐν ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"em amor\">ἐν ἀ.</span>:\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.16.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 16.14</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.3.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 3.17</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.4.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4.2</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.2.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 2.2</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.5.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ts 5.13</a>; compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.4.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 4.16</a> (sobre Ef 1.4, veja bα).\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐν τῇ ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"no amor\">ἐν τῇ ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 4.16b</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">18</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"διὰ τῆς ἀ. δουλεύετε ἀλλήλοις\" data-meanings=\"por meio do amor servi uns aos outros\">διὰ τῆς ἀ. δουλεύετε ἀλλήλοις</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.5.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gl 5.13</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"πίστις δι’ ἀγάπης ἐνεργουμένη\" data-meanings=\"fé operando por meio do amor\">πίστις δι’ ἀγάπης ἐνεργουμένη</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.5.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5.6</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"διὰ τὴν ἀ. παρακαλῶ\" data-meanings=\"por causa do amor, apelo\">διὰ τὴν ἀ. παρακαλῶ</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHM.1.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fm 9</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"μετὰ ἀγάπης πολιτεύεσθαι\" data-meanings=\"viver com amor\">μετὰ ἀγάπης πολιτεύεσθαι</span> 1 Cl 51:2. — Com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀλήθεια\" data-meanings=\"verdade\">ἀλήθεια</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2JN.1.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Jo 3</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"πίστις\" data-meanings=\"fé\">πίστις</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.3.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ts 3.6</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.5.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5.8</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.1.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Tm 1.14</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TI.1.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Tm 1.13</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHM.1.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fm 5</a>; B 11:8; IEph 1:1; 9:1; 14:1, entre outros. Com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"πίστις\" data-meanings=\"fé\">πίστις</span> e outros conceitos no mesmo nível:\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.6.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 6.23</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.2.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Tm 2.15</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.4.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4.12</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.6.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">6.11</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TI.2.22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Tm 2.22</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TI.3.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3.10</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/TIT.2.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tt 2.2</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.2.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ap 2.19</a>; Hm 8:9; compare v 3, 8, 2–5. A tríade <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"πίστις, ἐλπίς, ἀγάπη\" data-meanings=\"fé, esperança, amor\">πίστις, ἐλπίς, ἀγάπη</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.13.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 13.13</a>; veja também <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.1.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 1.4 s.</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.1.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ts 1.3</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.5.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5.8</a>; B 1:4 (compare Porfírio, <em>Ad Marcellam</em> 24\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τέσσαρα στοιχεῖα μάλιστα κεκρατύνθω περὶ θεοῦ· πίστις, ἀλήθεια, ἔρως, ἐλπίς\" data-meanings=\"quatro elementos sobretudo sejam fortalecidos acerca de Deus: fé, verdade, amor, esperança\">τέσσαρα στοιχεῖα μάλιστα κεκρατύνθω περὶ θεοῦ· πίστις, ἀλήθεια, ἔρως, ἐλπίς</span> e veja Rtzst., <em>Hist. Mon.</em> 1916, 242 ss.; <em>NGG</em> 1916, 367 ss.; 1917, 130 ss.; <em>Hist. Zeitschr.</em> 116, 1916, 189 ss.; A. Harnack, <em>PJ</em> 164, 1916, 5 ss. = <em>Aus d. Friedens-u. Kriegsarbeit</em> 1916, 1 ss.; P. Corssen, <em>Sokrates</em> 7, 1919, 18 ss.; A. Brieger, <em>D. urchr. Trias Gl., Lbe, Hoff.</em>, diss. Heidelberg 1925; W. Theiler, <em>D. Vorbereitung d. Neuplatonismus</em> 1930, 148 s.). Com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"δύναμις\" data-meanings=\"poder\">δύναμις</span> e <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"σωφρονισμός\" data-meanings=\"autodomínio|disciplina\">σωφρονισμός</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TI.1.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Tm 1.7</a>. Compare B 1:6. — Atributos do amor:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀνυπόκριτος\" data-meanings=\"sem hipocrisia|sincero\">ἀνυπόκριτος</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.12.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 12.9</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.6.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 6.6</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"γνησία\" data-meanings=\"genuíno\">γνησία</span> 1 Cl 62:2;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φιλόθεος\" data-meanings=\"amante de Deus\">φιλόθεος</span> e <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φιλάνθρωπος\" data-meanings=\"amigo dos seres humanos|humanitário\">φιλάνθρωπος</span> Agr 7;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"σύμφωνος\" data-meanings=\"harmonioso|concorde\">σύμφωνος</span> IEph 4:1;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄοκνος\" data-meanings=\"incansável\">ἄοκνος</span> IPol 7:2;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐκτενής\" data-meanings=\"intenso|constante\">ἐκτενής</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1PE.4.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Pe 4.8</a>. É fruto do Espírito:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"καρπὸς τοῦ πνεύματος\" data-meanings=\"fruto do Espírito\">καρπὸς τοῦ πνεύματος</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.5.22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gl 5.22</a>, e ocupa o primeiro lugar entre os frutos.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. τοῦ πνεύματος\" data-meanings=\"amor do Espírito\">ἀ. τοῦ πνεύματος</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.15.30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 15.30</a>; compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.1.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 1.8</a>. Como o termo denota preocupação por outro, o sentido <strong>esmola, caridade</strong> em ISm 6:2 é facilmente compreensível (compare <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. λαμβάνειν\" data-meanings=\"receber caridade|receber esmolas\">ἀ. λαμβάνειν</span> PGen 14, 7). — <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀσπάζεται ὑμᾶς ἡ ἀγάπη τῶν ἀδελφῶν\" data-meanings=\"o amor dos irmãos vos saúda\">ἀσπάζεται ὑμᾶς ἡ ἀγάπη τῶν ἀδελφῶν</span>,\n<em>os membros vos saúdam com amor</em>, IPhld 11:2; ISm 12:1; compare ITr 13:1; IRo 9:3. Nestas passagens, o objeto do amor muitas vezes é esclarecido pelo contexto; em outras é expressamente mencionado.\n<strong>β.</strong>\n<strong>א.</strong> Impessoal:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. τῆς ἀληθείας\" data-meanings=\"amor da verdade\">ἀ. τῆς ἀληθείας</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TH.2.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Ts 2.10</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. τῆς πατρίδος\" data-meanings=\"amor pela pátria\">ἀ. τῆς πατρίδος</span> 1 Cl 55:5.\n<strong>ב.</strong> Seres humanos:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. εἴς τινα\" data-meanings=\"amor por alguém\">ἀ. εἴς τινα</span>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"εἰς πάντας τοὺς ἁγίους\" data-meanings=\"por todos os santos\">εἰς πάντας τοὺς ἁγίους</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.1.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 1.15</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.1.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 1.4</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"εἰς ἀλλήλους καὶ εἰς πάντας\" data-meanings=\"uns pelos outros e por todos\">εἰς ἀλλήλους καὶ εἰς πάντας</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.3.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ts 3.12</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TH.1.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Ts 1.3</a>; compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.2.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 2.4</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.2.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">8</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1PE.4.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Pe 4.8</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2JN.1.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Jo 6</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐν ἀλλήλοις\" data-meanings=\"entre uns e outros\">ἐν ἀλλήλοις</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.13.35\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jo 13.35</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐξ ἡμῶν ἐν ὑμῖν\" data-meanings=\"de nós em vós\">ἐξ ἡμῶν ἐν ὑμῖν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.8.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 8.7</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἡ ἀ. μου μετὰ ὑμῶν\" data-meanings=\"meu amor esteja convosco\">ἡ ἀ. μου μετὰ ὑμῶν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.16.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 16.24</a>.\n<strong>ג.</strong> Deus ou Cristo (<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"πρὸς τὸν θεόν\" data-meanings=\"para com Deus\">πρὸς τὸν θεόν</span> Orígenes, <em>C. Cels.</em> 3, 15, 12):\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. τοῦ θεοῦ\" data-meanings=\"amor a Deus\">ἀ. τοῦ θεοῦ</span> (mas em muitos casos o genitivo pode ser subjetivo)\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.11.42\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lc 11.42</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.5.42\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jo 5.42</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TH.3.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Ts 3.5</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.2.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 2.5</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.2.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">15</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.3.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3.17</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4.12</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.5.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5.3</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.7.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 7.1</a> P46 (por <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φόβος\" data-meanings=\"temor\">φόβος</span>);\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. εἰς θεὸν καὶ Χριστὸν καὶ εἰς τὸν πλησίον\" data-meanings=\"amor por Deus e Cristo e pelo próximo\">ἀ. εἰς θεὸν καὶ Χριστὸν καὶ εἰς τὸν πλησίον</span> Pol 3:3;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. εἰς τὸ ὄνομα θεοῦ\" data-meanings=\"amor pelo nome de Deus\">ἀ. εἰς τὸ ὄνομα θεοῦ</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.6.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 6.10</a>.\n<strong>b.</strong> Do amor de Deus e de Cristo.\n<strong>α.</strong> Para seres humanos. De Deus (compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/WIS.3.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sb 3.9</a>):\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 4.10</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐν ἡμῖν\" data-meanings=\"em nós\">ἐν ἡμῖν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 4.9</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">16</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"εἰς ἡμᾶς\" data-meanings=\"para conosco\">εἰς ἡμᾶς</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.5.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 5.8</a>, compare v. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.5.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τετελείωται ἡ ἀ. μεθ’ ἡμῶν\" data-meanings=\"o amor foi aperfeiçoado conosco\">τετελείωται ἡ ἀ. μεθ’ ἡμῶν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 4.17</a> (veja H. Preisker, apêndice a H. Windisch, Comm. 167);\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀπὸ τῆς ἀ. τοῦ θεοῦ τῆς ἐν χριστῷ Ἰησοῦ\" data-meanings=\"do amor de Deus que está em Cristo Jesus\">ἀπὸ τῆς ἀ. τοῦ θεοῦ τῆς ἐν χριστῷ Ἰησοῦ</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.8.39\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 8.39</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγάπην διδόναι\" data-meanings=\"conceder amor\">ἀγάπην διδόναι</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.3.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 3.1</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐν ἀ. προορίσας ἡμᾶς εἰς υἱοθεσίαν\" data-meanings=\"em amor, predestinando-nos para adoção\">ἐν ἀ. προορίσας ἡμᾶς εἰς υἱοθεσίαν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.1.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 1.4 s.</a>: o ritmo da passagem sugere os crentes como agentes de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"amor\">ἀ.</span> no v. 4 (compare v. 15), mas <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.2.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2.4</a> favorece Deus; veja os comentários. — <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.13.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 13.13</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JUD.1.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jd 2</a> e <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JUD.1.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">21</a>. Deus é a fonte do amor, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 4.7</a>, o <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"θεὸς τῆς ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"Deus do amor\">θεὸς τῆς ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.13.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 13.11</a>, e portanto <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"θεὸς ἀγάπη ἐστίν\" data-meanings=\"Deus é amor\">θεὸς ἀγάπη ἐστίν</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 4.8</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">16</a>. Cristãos, envolvidos pelo amor de Deus, são <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τέκνα ἀγάπης\" data-meanings=\"filhos do amor\">τέκνα ἀγάπης</span> B 9:7; 21:9. — Do amor de Jesus:\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.15.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jo 15.9</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.15.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">10a</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.15.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">13</a> (veja M. Dibelius, “Joh 15:13”, <em>Deissmann Festschr.</em> 1927, 168–186);\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.3.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 3.16</a>. — <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.8.35\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 8.35</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.5.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 5.14</a>; compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.3.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 3.19</a>. Talvez o <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀληθὴς ἀγάπη\" data-meanings=\"amor verdadeiro\">ἀληθὴς ἀγάπη</span> de Pol 1:1 seja uma designação de Jesus ou de sua preocupação exemplar pelos outros.\n<strong>β.</strong> Da relação entre Deus e Cristo:\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.15.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jo 15.10b</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.17.26\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">17.26</a> (sobre a construção, compare Pel.-Leg. 12, 21 <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὁ πλοῦτος ὅν με ἐπλούτισεν ὁ σατανᾶς\" data-meanings=\"a riqueza com que Satanás me enriqueceu\">ὁ πλοῦτος ὅν με ἐπλούτισεν ὁ σατανᾶς</span>).\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τοῦ υἱοῦ τῆς ἀ. αὐτοῦ\" data-meanings=\"do Filho do seu amor\">τοῦ υἱοῦ τῆς ἀ. αὐτοῦ</span>,\n<em>do Filho do amor de Deus</em>, isto é, <em>do Filho amado de Deus</em>,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.1.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 1.13</a> (veja PsSol 13:9 <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"υἱὸς ἀγαπήσεως\" data-meanings=\"filho do amor\">υἱὸς ἀγαπήσεως</span>). — W. Lütgert, <em>D. L. im NT</em> 1905; B. Warfield, <em>PTR</em> 16, 1918, 1–45; 153–203; J. Moffatt, <em>Love in the NT</em> 1929; H. Preisker, <em>StKr</em> 95, 1924, 272–294; <em>D. urchr. Botschaft v. der L. Gottes</em> 1930; R. Schütz, <em>D. Vorgeschichte der joh. Formel ὁ θεὸς ἀγ. ἐστίν</em>, diss. Kiel 1917; C. Bowen, “Love in the Fourth Gosp.”, <em>JR</em> 13, 1933, 39–49; G. Eichholz, “Glaube u. L. im 1 J”, <em>EvTh</em> 1937, 411–437. Sobre <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἔρως\" data-meanings=\"eros|amor\">ἔρως</span> e <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"ágape|amor\">ἀ.</span>, veja Harnack, <em>SBBerlAk</em> 1918, 81–94; A. Nygren, <em>Eros u. Agape</em> I 1930, II 1937 (trad. ingl. <em>Agape and Eros</em>, A. Hebert e P. Watson 1932, 1939; sobre esta, J. Robinson, <em>Theology</em> 48, 1945, 98–104); L. Grünhut, <em>Eros u. Ag.</em> 1931. Compare C. Tarelli, “Ἀγάπη”, <em>JTS</em> n.s. 1, 1950, 64–67; E. Lee, “Love and Righteousness”, <em>ET</em> 62, 1950/51, 28–31; A. Šuštar, <em>Verbum Domini</em> 28, 1950, 110–119; 122–140; 193–213; 257–270; 321–340; T. Ohm, <em>D. Liebe zu Gott in d. nichtchristl. Religionen</em>, 1950; W. Harrelson, “The Idea of Agape”, <em>JR</em> 31, 1951, 169–182; V. Warnach, <em>Agape: Die Liebe als Grundmotiv der ntl. Theol.</em> 1951; J. Steinmueller, “Ἐρᾶν, Φιλεῖν, Ἀγαπᾶν in Extrabiblical and Bibl. Sources”, <em>Studia Anselmiana</em> 27 s., 1951, 404–423. — Bibliografia completa em H. Riesenfeld, “Étude bibliographique sur la notion biblique d’ἀγάπη, surtout dans 1 Cor 13”, <em>ConNeot</em> 5, 1941, 1–32; veja também EDNT.\n<span class=\"sense-number\">2.</span>\n<strong>Uma refeição comum tomada pelos primeiros cristãos em conexão com seu culto, com o propósito de fomentar e expressar afeição e preocupação mútuas, refeição de comunhão, uma festa de amor</strong> (os detalhes não são discutidos no NT, embora Paulo se refira a ela implicitamente em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.11.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 11.17 ss.</a>; compare D 9–10; veja também Plínio, <em>Ep.</em> 10, 96, 7; AcPlTh 25 [Aa I 252]; Clemente de Alexandria, <em>Paed.</em> 2, 1, 4; <em>Strom.</em> 3, 2, 10;\n<em>Pass. Perp. et Felic.</em> 17, 1; Tertuliano, <em>Apolog.</em> 39; <em>De Jejun.</em> 17; Minúcio Félix 31):\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JUD.1.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jd 12</a> (v.l. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀπάταις\" data-meanings=\"enganos\">ἀπάταις</span>; em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.2.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pe 2.13</a> <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγάπαις\" data-meanings=\"ágapes|festas de amor\">ἀγάπαις</span> é v.l. de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀπάταις\" data-meanings=\"enganos\">ἀπάταις</span>; a mesma v.l. em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/ECC.9.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ec 9.6</a>, onde <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀπάτη\" data-meanings=\"engano\">ἀπάτη</span> no ms. S não faz sentido: veja R. Schütz, <em>ZNW</em> 18, 1918, 224; veja <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπάω\" data-meanings=\"amar\">ἀγαπάω</span> 3 sobre Jo 13.1, 34).\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγάπη ἄφθαρτος\" data-meanings=\"amor incorruptível\">ἀγάπη ἄφθαρτος</span> IRo 7:3.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγάπην ποιεῖν\" data-meanings=\"realizar uma ágape|fazer uma refeição de amor\">ἀγάπην ποιεῖν</span>,\n<em>realizar uma festa de amor</em>, ISm 8:2; em ambas as passagens, com provável referência à eucaristia (veja <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπάω\" data-meanings=\"amar\">ἀγαπάω</span> 2 e 3). — Refeições acompanhadas de ritos religiosos e num contexto religioso eram realizadas por diversos grupos sociais entre os gregos desde tempos antigos (veja a Introdução de Bauer, pp. xxvii–xxviii, acima). Um escólio a Platão 122b diz de tais refeições entre os lacedemônios que eram chamadas\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φιλίτια\" data-meanings=\"refeições comunitárias espartanas\">φιλίτια</span>, porque <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φιλίας συναγωγά ἐστιν\" data-meanings=\"são reuniões de amizade\">φιλίας συναγωγά ἐστιν</span>. Seria <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγ.\" data-meanings=\"ἀγάπη\">ἀγ.</span> talvez uma tradução de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φιλία\" data-meanings=\"amizade\">φιλία</span> para terminologia cristã? — J. Keating, <em>The Ag. and the Eucharist in the Early Church</em> 1901; H. Leclercq, <em>Dict. d’Arch.</em> I 1903, 775–848; F. Funk, <em>Kirchengesch. Abhdlgen.</em> 3, 1907, 1–41; E. Baumgartner, <em>Eucharistie u. Ag. im Urchr.</em> 1909; R. Cole, <em>Love Feasts, a History of the Christian Ag.</em> 1916; G. Wetter, <em>Altchr. Liturgien</em> II 1921; H. Lietzmann, <em>Messe u. Herrenmahl</em> 1926 (sobre este, A. Loisy, <em>Congr. d’Hist. du Christ.</em> I 1928, 77–95); K. Völker, <em>Mysterium u. Ag.</em> 1927; D. Tambolleo, <em>Le Agapi</em> 1931; B. Reicke, <em>Diakonie, Festfreude u. Zelos in Verbindung mit der altchristlichen Agapenfeier</em>, 1951. — T. Söding, “Das Wortfeld der Liebe im paganen und biblischen Griechisch”, <em>ETL</em> 68, 1992, 284–330. — DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπάω\" data-meanings=\"amar\">ἀγαπάω</span>. <span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"M-M\" data-tooltip-text=\"Moulton-Milligan, The Vocabulary of the Greek Testament\">M-M</span>. <span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"TW\" data-tooltip-text=\"Theologisches Wörterbuch zum Neuen Testament\">TW</span>. <span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"Spicq\" data-tooltip-text=\"Ceslas Spicq, Notes de lexicographie néo-testamentaire\">Spicq</span>. TRE s.v. Liebe.\n</p>\n</section>\n</article><article id=\"entry-agapetos-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">ἀγαπητός</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"greek\">ή, όν</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦agapētós⟧</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span>adjetivo verbal</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Adjetivo verbal de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπάω\" data-meanings=\"amar\">ἀγαπάω</span>, fixado como adjetivo:\n<span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"B-D-F §65, 3\" data-tooltip-text=\"Blass-Debrunner-Funk, §65, 3\">B-D-F §65, 3</span>; Rob. 1096.) “<strong>Amado</strong>”.\n<span class=\"sense-number\">1.</span>\n<strong>Relativo a alguém que está numa relação muito especial com outro, único, unicamente amado</strong>, com referência a um filho único (comum desde Homero; Pólux 3, 19 <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"καλοῖτο ἂν υἱὸς ἀγ. ὁ μόνος ὢν πατρί\" data-meanings=\"poderia ser chamado filho amado aquele que é o único para o pai\">καλοῖτο ἂν υἱὸς ἀγ. ὁ μόνος ὢν πατρί</span>; LXX [<bdi class=\"hebrew hebrew-token tooltip-trigger\" lang=\"he\" dir=\"rtl\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"hebrew\" data-tooltip-label=\"יָחִיד\" data-transliteration=\"yāḥîḏ\" data-meanings=\"único|filho único\">יָחִיד</bdi>]\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.22.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gn 22.2</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.22.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">12</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.22.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">16</a>, entre outros; ParJer 7:24 [Baruc]; AscIs 3:13, 17, 18; 4:3; 7:24 [Baruc]; substantivado <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὁ ἀγαπητός\" data-meanings=\"o amado\">ὁ ἀγαπητός</span>; Fílon, <em>Ebr.</em> 30 <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"μόνος κ. ἀγ. υἱός\" data-meanings=\"filho único e amado\">μόνος κ. ἀγ. υἱός</span>). Da relação de Cristo com Deus (compare a interpolação em TestBenj 11:2):\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὁ υἱός μου ὁ ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"meu Filho amado\">ὁ υἱός μου ὁ ἀ.</span>\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.3.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 3.17</a> (B. Bacon, “Jesus’ Voice fr. Heaven”, <em>AJT</em> 9, 1905, 451–473) = GEb 18, 39;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.17.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 17.5</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.1.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mc 1.11</a> = GEb 18, 37;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.9.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mc 9.7</a>, compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.12.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">12.6</a> (C. Turner, <em>JTS</em> 27, 1926, 113–129; 28, 1927, 362, traduziria “único”; veja A. Souter, ibid. 28, 1927, 59 s.);\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.3.22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lc 3.22</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.9.35\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">9.35</a> v.l.; compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.20.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">20.13</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.1.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pe 1.17</a>. — <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.12.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 12.18</a>; MPol 14:1, 3; Dg 8:11.\n<span class=\"sense-number\">2.</span>\n<strong>Relativo a alguém que é ternamente amado, querido, amado, prezado, estimado</strong> (papiros, LXX, pseudoepígrafos;\n<a class=\"biblio-ref reference-link tooltip-trigger\" href=\"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=urn%3Acts%3AgreekLit%3Atlg0526.tlg004.perseus-grc1%3A1.240\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"Jos., Bell. 1, 240\" data-tooltip-text=\"Flávio Josefo, Guerra Judaica 1.240 — texto grego original no Perseus Digital Library; destino validado\">Jos., Bell. 1, 240</a>;\n<a class=\"biblio-ref reference-link tooltip-trigger\" href=\"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=urn%3Acts%3AgreekLit%3Atlg0526.tlg001.perseus-grc1%3A15.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"Ant. 15, 15\" data-tooltip-text=\"Flávio Josefo, Antiguidades Judaicas 15.15 — texto grego original no Perseus Digital Library; destino validado\">Ant. 15, 15</a>; Melito, <em>P.</em> 2, 7), indicando uma relação estreita, especialmente entre pai/mãe e filho:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"υἱός\" data-meanings=\"filho\">υἱός</span> (TestAbr A 83, 31 s. [Stone p. 14]; Artemidoro 5, 37) Hs 5, 2, 6. Com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τέκνον\" data-meanings=\"filho|criança\">τέκνον</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.4.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 4.17</a>,\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τέκνα\" data-meanings=\"filhos\">τέκνα</span> v. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.4.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">14</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.5.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 5.1</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀδελφός\" data-meanings=\"irmão\">ἀδελφός</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHM.1.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fm 16</a>. Com nomes próprios (POxy 235, 2 [séc. I a.C.] <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"Τρύφων ἀγαπητέ\" data-meanings=\"querido Trifão\">Τρύφων ἀγαπητέ</span>):\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.16.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 16.12</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHM.1.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fm 1</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.15.25\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">At 15.25</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/3JN.1.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3 Jo 1</a>; com nomes próprios e <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀδελφός\" data-meanings=\"irmão\">ἀδελφός</span>\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.6.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ef 6.21</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.4.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 4.7</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.4.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">9</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.3.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pe 3.15</a>; com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"σύνδουλος\" data-meanings=\"conservo\">σύνδουλος</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.1.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 1.7</a>; com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τέκνον\" data-meanings=\"filho\">τέκνον</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TI.1.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Tm 1.2</a>; com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἰατρός\" data-meanings=\"médico\">ἰατρός</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.4.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cl 4.14</a>; com genitivo do pronome pessoal e nome próprio:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"Ἐπαίνετον τὸν ἀ. μου\" data-meanings=\"Epêneto, meu amado\">Ἐπαίνετον τὸν ἀ. μου</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.16.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 16.5</a>; compare vv. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.16.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">8 s.</a>; IPol 8:2. — Frequentemente em tratamento direto (Hipólito, <em>Ref.</em> 4, 50, 1):\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπητέ\" data-meanings=\"amado|querido amigo\">ἀγαπητέ</span>, <em>querido amigo</em>,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/3JN.1.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3 Jo 2</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/3JN.1.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">5</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/3JN.1.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">11</a> (compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/TOB.10.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tb 10.13</a>); principalmente plural <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπητοί\" data-meanings=\"amados\">ἀγαπητοί</span>\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.12.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 12.19</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.7.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Co 7.1</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.12.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">12.19</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.6.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 6.9</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1PE.2.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Pe 2.11</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1PE.4.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4.12</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.3.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pe 3.1</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.3.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">8</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.3.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">14</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.3.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">17</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.2.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 2.7</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.3.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">3.2</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.3.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">21</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4.1</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">7</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.4.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">11</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JUD.1.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jd 3</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JUD.1.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">17</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JUD.1.20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">20</a>; 1 Cl 1:1; 7:1; 12:8; 21:1; 24:1 s., entre outros.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. μου\" data-meanings=\"meus amados\">ἀ. μου</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.10.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 10.14</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.2.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fp 2.12</a>; IMg 11:1.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄνδρες ἀγαπητοί\" data-meanings=\"homens amados\">ἄνδρες ἀγαπητοί</span>, <em>queridas pessoas</em>, 1 Cl 16:17.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀδελφοί μου ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"meus irmãos amados\">ἀδελφοί μου ἀ.</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.15.58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Co 15.58</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.1.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tg 1.16</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.1.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">19</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.2.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2.5</a>;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀδελφοί μου ἀ. καὶ ἐπιπόθητοι\" data-meanings=\"meus irmãos amados e saudosos\">ἀδελφοί μου ἀ. καὶ ἐπιπόθητοι</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.4.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fp 4.1</a>. — De membros de um grupo cristão:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. θεοῦ\" data-meanings=\"amados de Deus\">ἀ. θεοῦ</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.1.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 1.7</a> (compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/PSA.59.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sl 59.7</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/PSA.107.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">107.7</a>; ApcEsdr 1:1 p. 24, 3 [Esdras]).\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"(Παῦλον) τὸν ἀγαπητόν τοῦ κυρίου\" data-meanings=\"(Paulo), o amado do Senhor\">(Παῦλον) τὸν ἀγαπητόν τοῦ κυρίου</span> AcPl Ha 8, 2. Os israelitas são, <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"κατὰ τὴν ἐκλογὴν ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"quanto à eleição, amados\">κατὰ τὴν ἐκλογὴν ἀ.</span>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.11.28\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rm 11.28</a>. Dos profetas, IPhld 9:2. — <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγαπητοὶ ἡμῖν ἐγενήθητε\" data-meanings=\"vos tornastes queridos para nós\">ἀγαπητοὶ ἡμῖν ἐγενήθητε</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.2.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ts 2.8</a>; compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.6.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Tm 6.2</a> (talvez = “digno de amor”, como Xenofonte, <em>Mem.</em> 3, 10, 5);\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. λίαν ἔχειν τινά\" data-meanings=\"ter alguém como muito querido\">ἀ. λίαν ἔχειν τινά</span>, <em>ter alguém em grande estima</em>, IPol 7:2. — E. H. van Leeuwen, “Ἀγαπητοί”, <em>ThStud</em> 21, 1903, 139–151. — <em>New Docs</em> 4, 252. <span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"M-M\" data-tooltip-text=\"Moulton-Milligan, The Vocabulary of the Greek Testament\">M-M</span>. <span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"TW\" data-tooltip-text=\"Theologisches Wörterbuch zum Neuen Testament\">TW</span>.\n</p>\n</section>\n</article><article id=\"entry-hagar-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">Ἁγάρ</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"article greek\">ἡ</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦Hagár⟧</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span>indeclinável</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Bov., N.; <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"Ἀγάρ\" data-meanings=\"Agar\">Ἀγάρ</span> M.; <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"Ἄγαρ\" data-meanings=\"Agar\">Ἄγαρ</span> t.r., Tdf., S., Vog.; <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"Ἅγαρ\" data-meanings=\"Agar\">Ἅγαρ</span> W-H. —\n<bdi class=\"hebrew hebrew-token tooltip-trigger\" lang=\"he\" dir=\"rtl\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"hebrew\" data-tooltip-label=\"הָגָר\" data-transliteration=\"hāḡār\" data-meanings=\"Agar|nome próprio feminino\">הָגָר</bdi>.) Indeclinável (LXX, Fílon. — Em\n<a class=\"biblio-ref reference-link tooltip-trigger\" href=\"https://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text?doc=urn%3Acts%3AgreekLit%3Atlg0526.tlg001.perseus-grc1%3A1.215\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"Jos., Ant. 1, 215\" data-tooltip-text=\"Flávio Josefo, Antiguidades Judaicas 1.215 — texto grego original no Perseus Digital Library; destino validado\">Jos., Ant. 1, 215</a>,\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"Ἁγάρη, ης\" data-meanings=\"Agar; forma declinada em Josefo\">Ἁγάρη, ης</span>.)\n<strong>Agar</strong>, concubina de Abraão, mãe de Ismael (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.16.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gn 16</a>); tomada alegoricamente por Paulo como tipo do judaísmo,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.4.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gl 4.24</a>. No v. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.4.25\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">25</a>,\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τὸ δὲ Ἁγὰρ Σινᾶ ὄρος ἐστὶν ἐν τῇ Ἀραβίᾳ\" data-meanings=\"Agar é o monte Sinai na Arábia\">τὸ δὲ Ἁγὰρ Σινᾶ ὄρος ἐστὶν ἐν τῇ Ἀραβίᾳ</span>, as leituras dos manuscritos variam consideravelmente (Zahn, <em>Gal.</em> exc. II p. 296–299). Talvez haja aqui um jogo de nomes, pois o árabe <em>ḥajar</em> (ou <em>ḥadschar, ḥaǧar</em>) significa “pedra”, e nomes compostos com ele são encontrados na península do Sinai. O sentido é: Agar é um tipo da lei mosaica, pois <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"Ἁγάρ = Σινᾶ\" data-meanings=\"Agar = Sinai\">Ἁγάρ = Σινᾶ</span>. — <span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"TW\" data-tooltip-text=\"Theologisches Wörterbuch zum Neuen Testament\">TW</span>.\n</p>\n</section>\n</article><article id=\"entry-angareuo-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">ἀγγαρεύω</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦angareúō⟧</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"greek\">fut. ἀγγαρεύσω; 1 aor. ἠγγάρευσα</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Cognato de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγαρος\" data-meanings=\"mensageiro do correio real; termo persa\">ἄγγαρος</span>, termo persa para mensageiros reais [R. Schmitt, <em>Glotta</em> 49, 1971, 97 ss.; B-D-F §6], mais tarde de correios nacionais montados [= <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγγαρήιον\" data-meanings=\"serviço de correio; correio oficial\">ἀγγαρήιον</span> Hdt 8, 98]; empréstimo em Aeschyl., <em>Ag.</em> 282; Hdt 3, 126, com derivação do verbo no grego helenístico: Menand. <em>Fgm.</em> 373 Kö. = <em>Sicyon Fgm.</em> 4 S. p. 285; em papiros desde 257 a.C. [Mayser I<sup>1</sup> p. 42 e I<sup>2</sup>, 3 p. 139, 3; também PCairZen 509, 5]; OGI 665, 24; Jos., <em>Ant.</em> 13, 52. Para a v.l. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἐγγαρεύω\" data-meanings=\"forma variante de ἀγγαρεύω\">ἐγγαρεύω</span>, veja B-D-F §42, 2; Mlt-H. 67. Também na literatura rabínica [P. Fiebig, ZNW 18, 1920, 64–72] e em latim como <em>angariare</em>: Ulpian, <em>Dig.</em> XLIX 18, 4.)\n<strong>Requisitar</strong> (originalmente, para o correio oficial no período helenístico),\n<strong>pressionar para o serviço</strong> e, assim, <strong>forçar, compelir</strong>, com objeto:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τοῦτον ἠγγάρευσαν, ἵνα ἄρῃ τὸν σταυρόν\" data-meanings=\"eles o obrigaram ao serviço para que carregasse a cruz\">τοῦτον ἠγγάρευσαν, ἵνα ἄρῃ τὸν σταυρόν</span>, “obrigaram-no ao serviço para carregar a cruz”,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.27.32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 27.32</a>; compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.15.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mc 15.21</a>.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὅστις σε ἀγγαρεύσει μίλιον ἕν\" data-meanings=\"quem te obrigar a percorrer uma milha\">ὅστις σε ἀγγαρεύσει μίλιον ἕν</span> (subentenda-se <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὑπάγειν\" data-meanings=\"ir; percorrer\">ὑπάγειν</span>), “quem te obrigar a percorrer uma milha”,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.5.41\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 5.41</a>;\n<span class=\"biblio-ref tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"biblio\" data-tooltip-label=\"D 1:4\" data-tooltip-text=\"Didaquê 1:4 — referência da obra cristã antiga abreviada no BDAG\">D 1:4</span>. — F. Oertel, <em>Die Liturgie</em> 1917, 24 ss.; H. Pflaum, <em>Essai sur le cursus publicus</em>, <em>Mém. Acad. Insc. et Bell. Lettr.</em> 14, 1940, 1 ss.; M. Rostovtzeff, <em>Klio</em> 6, 1906, 249 ss.; Wilcken, <em>Grundzüge</em> 372 ss., APF 4, 1908, 228; F. Zucker, SBBerlAk 1911, 803 ss.; F. Preisigke, <em>Klio</em> 7, 1907, 241 ss., <em>Fachwörter</em> 1915; S. Mitchell, JRS 66, 1976, 106–131 (nova inscrição da Pisídia). — DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγαρος\" data-meanings=\"mensageiro do correio real; termo persa\">ἄγγαρος</span>.\n<em>New Docs</em> 1, 42; 2, 77. M-M. Spicq.\n</p>\n</section>\n</article><article id=\"entry-angeion-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">ἀγγεῖον</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"greek\">ου, τό</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦angeîon⟧</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Hdt.+; inscrições, papiros, LXX.)\n<strong>Vaso, frasco, recipiente</strong>, por exemplo para óleo (PColZen 21, 2 [séc. III a.C.]; BGU 248, 40 [séc. I d.C.];\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/NUM.4.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nm 4.9</a>; Fílon; Jos., <em>Bell.</em> 3, 272; <em>Ant.</em> 9, 48):\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.25.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 25.4</a>. De recipientes para peixe (compare PSI 553, 11 [séc. III a.C.], para caracóis comestíveis),\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.13.48\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 13.48</a> v.l. de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγη\" data-meanings=\"recipientes; forma variante\">ἄγγη</span>. Figuradamente, do corpo (Hipócrates e outros; Dio Chrys. 11 [12], 59; M. Ant. 3, 3, 6; Stob. I 414, 9; Fílon, <em>Post. Cain.</em> 137, <em>Migr. Abr.</em> 193; 197) como morada de espíritos (com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγος\" data-meanings=\"vaso; recipiente\">ἄγγος</span>) Hm 5, 2, 5. Veja <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγος\" data-meanings=\"vaso; recipiente\">ἄγγος</span>. — DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγος\" data-meanings=\"vaso; recipiente\">ἄγγος</span>. M-M.\n</p>\n</section>\n</article><article id=\"entry-angelia-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">ἀγγελία</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"greek\">ας, ἡ</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦angelía⟧</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Hom. e outros; LXX.)\n<span class=\"sense-number\">1.</span>\n<strong>Mensagem</strong> (Jos., <em>Ant.</em> 17, 332; <em>Vi.</em> 380; TestNapht 2:1);\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀ. ἀγαθή\" data-meanings=\"boa mensagem; boa notícia\">ἀ. ἀγαθή</span> (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/PRO.12.25\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pv 12.25</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/PRO.25.25\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">25.25</a>),\n<strong>boa notícia</strong>, Hv 3, 13, 2; do evangelho, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.1.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 1.5</a>, com o conteúdo indicado por oração com <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὅτι\" data-meanings=\"que; introduz o conteúdo da mensagem\">ὅτι</span>.\n<span class=\"sense-number\">2.</span>\n<strong>Instrução, diretriz</strong> para amar os companheiros em Cristo,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1JN.3.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Jo 3.11</a>, seguida de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἵνα\" data-meanings=\"para que; introduz oração de finalidade ou conteúdo\">ἵνα</span>. — DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγελος\" data-meanings=\"mensageiro; anjo\">ἄγγελος</span>. M-M. TW.\n</p>\n</section>\n</article><article id=\"entry-angelikos-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">ἀγγελικός</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"greek\">ή, όν</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦angelikós⟧</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Pollux 4, 103.)\n<strong>Relativo a um mensageiro celestial, angélico</strong>:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τῇ ἀ. διαλέκτῳ\" data-meanings=\"em linguagem angélica\">τῇ ἀ. διαλέκτῳ</span> TestJob 48:3;\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τῆς ἀ. στρατιᾶς\" data-meanings=\"do exército angélico\">τῆς ἀ. στρατιᾶς</span> Just., <em>A</em> I, 52, 3;\n<em>Theosophien</em> 14 p. 170, 11; Hierocles 2, 423; Proclus sobre Pla., <em>Rep.</em>, índice de Kroll; escólio sobre Pla. 216a; Simplicius em Epict. p. 42, 53\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀρεταὶ ἀγγελικαί\" data-meanings=\"virtudes angélicas\">ἀρεταὶ ἀγγελικαί</span>; 45, 54; 80, 7.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τοποθεσίαι ἀ.\" data-meanings=\"lugares dos anjos\">τοποθεσίαι ἀ.</span> “lugares dos anjos”, ITr 5:2.\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"φοβοῦμαι μήπως ἀγγελικόν ‹ἐστιν τὸ› ἐν ἑαυτῇ\" data-meanings=\"temo que aquilo que está nela seja de origem angélica\">φοβοῦμαι μήπως ἀγγελικόν ‹ἐστιν τὸ› ἐν ἑαυτῇ</span>, “temo que aquilo que está nela seja de origem angélica”, GJs 14:1 de Strycker (compare <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.6.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gn 6.1</a>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.6.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">4</a>; En 106:6, 12; Jubileus 5:1–12). — A restauração de J. Bartlet em Ox 1081, 34 é insustentável (SJCh 90, 12 lê <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγένητος\" data-meanings=\"não gerado; não criado, conforme a leitura citada\">ἀγένητος</span>; veja <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀγέννητος\" data-meanings=\"não nascido; não gerado\">ἀγέννητος</span>).\n</p>\n</section>\n</article><article id=\"entry-angello-bdag\" class=\"entry-card\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\">\n<header class=\"entry-header\">\n<div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">ἀγγέλλω</h1>\n<div class=\"entry-meta\"><span class=\"transliteration\">⟦angéllō⟧</span><span class=\"separator\">·</span><span class=\"greek\">1 aor. ἤγγειλα</span></div>\n</div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div>\n</header>\n<div class=\"entry-divider\"></div>\n<section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução literal</div>\n<p class=\"entry-text\"> (Hom.+; inscrições; papiros [raramente]; LXX em diversas passagens, por exemplo <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/JER.4.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jr 4.15</a> como v.l.; Jos., <em>Vi.</em> 301, entre outros; Just.)\n<strong>Anunciar</strong>, <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"τινί\" data-meanings=\"a alguém\">τινί</span> “a alguém”: da mensagem pascal levada por Maria Madalena,\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.20.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jo 20.18</a>;\n<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.51\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jo 4.51</a> v.l. de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"λέγοντες\" data-meanings=\"dizendo\">λέγοντες</span>, também com v.l. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀπ-\" data-meanings=\"prefixo ἀπ- na forma variante\">ἀπ-</span> e v.l. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀν-\" data-meanings=\"prefixo ἀν- na forma variante\">ἀν-</span>, seguida de <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ὅτι\" data-meanings=\"que\">ὅτι</span>; GJs 6:3. — Veja também <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀναγγέλλω\" data-meanings=\"anunciar; comunicar\">ἀναγγέλλω</span> 1, final, e <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἀπαγγέλλω\" data-meanings=\"anunciar; relatar\">ἀπαγγέλλω</span>. AcPl Ha 2, 15:\n<span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"καὶ ἀπελθοῦ|[σα ἤγγει]λ̣εν τῷ Παύλῳ\" data-meanings=\"e, tendo partido, anunciou a Paulo\">καὶ ἀπελθοῦ|[σα ἤγγει]λ̣εν τῷ Παύλῳ</span>. — B. 1278. DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek greek-term tooltip-trigger\" tabindex=\"0\" data-tooltip-type=\"greek\" data-tooltip-label=\"ἄγγελος\" data-meanings=\"mensageiro; anjo\">ἄγγελος</span>. M-M. TW.\n</p>\n</section>\n</article>"};
